#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180768 :tutorial/content "Let's remind ourselves of the three rules for dividing with negative numbers:\n\n- A negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number.\n$(-)\\div(+) = (-)$\n- A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number.\n$(+)\\div(-) = (-)$\n- A negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number.\n$(-)\\div(-) = (+)$" :tutorial/id #uuid "19bbbf1e-a31e-54b1-92bb-a2fb71bf54b8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8022 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180769 :tutorial/content "As an example, let's find the value of\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-4)\n$$\n\nDividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n2.4\\div 4=0.6\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-4) = -0.6\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3c2ea5e2-fa57-573b-8e38-712b30958ca4" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8023 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"}]}
